EDICT 0011: GetWavinfo reads no cue length marker past the end of the file

Category: undefined behaviour pinned, no change in results (the sound build, build.sh SOUND=1).
After a cue chunk GetWavinfo takes the next LIST chunk for cooledit's "mark" and compares the four bytes 28 bytes
into it, without checking that they are in the file. Six of LibreQuake's sounds (plats/medplat1, plats/train1,
doors/winch2, doors/stndr1, doors/airdoor1, doors/doormv1) end in a LIST chunk of 4 bytes: the compare reads 16 to
19 bytes past the file, which COM_LoadStackFile put at the top of the hunk, so past the hunk's memory (AddressSanitizer
stops there). The bytes are whatever lies there; in every run so far they were not "mark". Now bytes past the file
are never "mark", as the port reads them (0, COM_LoadFile's terminator and beyond).

--- a/snd_mem.c
+++ b/snd_mem.c
@@ -303,7 +303,8 @@
 		FindNextChunk ("LIST");
 		if (data_p)
 		{
-			if (!strncmp (data_p + 28, "mark", 4))
+			// EDICT: bytes past the file are not "mark" (patch 0011)
+			if (data_p + 32 <= iff_end && !strncmp (data_p + 28, "mark", 4))
 			{	// this is not a proper parse, but it works with cooledit...
 				data_p += 24;
 				i = GetLittleLong ();	// samples in loop
